#==============================================================================================
#
#   rule_parsing_1 - converting parsed rules to CSSOM rules: DescriptorList, convert_to_rule,
#                    style rules, @import and <layer-name>
#
#   DESCRIPTION:
#       Port of LibWeb/CSS/Parser/RuleParsing.cpp (lines 1-356): the DescriptorList helper
#       class, convert_to_rule (dispatching on the at-rule's name), convert_to_style_rule,
#       convert_to_import_rule and parse_layer_name.
#
#       convert_to_rule and the rule converters it reaches are templates over the rule type
#       that holds nested declarations (CSSNestedDeclarations, or CSSFunctionDeclarations
#       inside @function), which they create with `NestedDeclarationsRule::create(...)`. A
#       luce-base generic cannot call a static function of its type parameter, so
#       css_parser_create_nested_declarations_rule tells the two types apart by size (they
#       differ, which a module assert checks), the way parser_2's per-T steps do for tokens.
#
